  "food": {
    "title": "Food on the Nador Corniche",
    "p1": "The corniche is the easiest place to eat with a lagoon view — seafood grills, cafés and simple evening tables as the promenade fills up.",
    "li1": "Seafood restaurants along the lagoon-facing stretch.",
    "li2": "Cafés for tea, juice and sunset watching.",
    "li3": "Grilled fish and salads for a light dinner.",
    "li4": "Busy tables are often a safer quality signal.",
    "li5": "Walk beyond the first row of cafés to compare options.",
    "p2": "Evenings are livelier than midday on the waterfront."
  },
